{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-117133",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Let's add the graph of $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ to the plot.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14255079/assets/d454fce5ce753dada69e9c927279237760cb32434cb4743bad04c62f10798cc9.png)\n\nTo plot the given curve, we follow these steps:\n\n- Start with the graph of $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$\n\n- Then, shift it by $\\frac{3}{4}$ unit **right.**\n\nTherefore, the given graph is $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-\\frac{3}{4}).$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
